cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VULYK, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "VULYK: Hive Orchestration for Claude Code"
abstract: >-
  VULYK is a model-cascade, memory-first, self-evolving framework for running
  multi-agent coding at scale on Anthropic's Claude Code, built entirely on
  native Claude Code primitives (subagents, slash commands, skills, hooks,
  rules). It routes each task to the cheapest capable model tier (queen, leads,
  workers, drones), keeps shared state in a git-based external memory plane
  instead of the context window, and turns session learnings into reviewable
  configuration pull requests.
type: software
